[167.953377, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m17\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[167.953782, "o", "\r\u001b[2KKLEE reports STP as the default solver. Before testing, I need to update `~/.bashrc` carefully: Ubuntu's default `.bashrc` returns early for non-interactive \r\nshells, so I'll insert the environment exports at the top to guarantee they load when tests source the file.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnl -ba ~/.bashrc | sed -n '1,30p'; echo '--- test sample'; cat >/tmp/test_klee.c <<'EOF'\r\n#include <klee/klee.h>\r\n\r\nint main(void) {\r\n  int x;\r\n  klee_make_symbolic(&x, sizeof(x), \"x\");\r\n  if (x == 5) {\r\n    klee_assert(0);\r\n  }\r\n  return 0;\r\n}\r\nEOF\r\nclang-16 -I/usr/local/include -emit-llvm -c -g -O0 -Xclang -disable-O0-optnone /tmp/test_klee.c -o /tmp/test_klee.bc && echo compiled; rm -rf /tmp/klee-out-0; \r\ncd /tmp && /usr/local/bin/klee --solver-backend=stp --stp-sat-solver=minisat --output-dir=/tmp/klee-out-0 /tmp/test_klee.bc; echo RC=$?; find /tmp/klee-out-0 \r\n-maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f\\n' | sort; grep -E 'KLEE:|Error|error|assert' /tmp/klee-out-0/messages.txt 2>/dev/null || true\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[167.955689, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[168.020943, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[168.023235, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n     1  # ~/.bashrc: executed by bash(1) for non-login shells.\r\n     2  # see /usr/share/doc/bash/examples/startup-files (in the package bash-doc)\r\n     3  # for examples\r\n     4  \r\n     5  # If not running interactively, don't do anything\r\n     6  [ -z \"$PS1\" ] && return\r\n     7  \r\n     8  # don't put duplicate lines in the history. See bash(1) for more options\r\n     9  # ... or force ignoredups and ignorespace\r\n    10  HISTCONTROL=ignoredups:ignorespace\r\n    11  \r\n    12  # append to the history file, don't overwrite it\r\n    13  shopt -s histappend\r\n    14  \r\n    15  # for setting history length see HISTSIZE and HISTFILESIZE in bash(1)\r\n    16  HISTSIZE=1000\r\n    17  HISTFILESIZE=2000\r\n    18  \r\n    19  # check the window size after each command and, if necessary,\r\n    20  # update the values of LINES and COLUMNS.\r\n    21  shopt -s checkwinsize\r\n    22  \r\n    23  # make less more friendly for non-text input files, see lesspipe(1)\r\n    24  [ -x /usr/bin/lesspipe ] && eval \"$(SHELL=/bin/sh lesspipe)\"\r\n    25  \r\n    26  # set variable identifying the chroot you work in (used in the prompt below)\r\n    27  if [ -z \"$debian_chroot\" ] && [ -r /etc/debian_chroot ]; then"]
[168.023334, "o", "\r\n    28      debian_chroot=$(cat /etc/debian_chroot)\r\n    29  fi\r\n    30  \r\n--- test sample\r\ncompiled\r\nKLEE: output directory is \"/tmp/klee-out-0\"\r\nKLEE: Using STP solver backend\r\nKLEE: SAT solver: MiniSat\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: Using quarantine queue size 8\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: globals (start-address=0xe91368e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: constants (start-address=0xe910e8e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: heap (start-address=0xe810e8e00000 size=1024 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: stack (start-address=0xe7f0e8e00000 size=128 GiB)\r\nKLEE: ERROR: /tmp/test_klee.c:7: ASSERTION FAIL: 0\r\nKLEE: NOTE: now ignoring this error at this location\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: Using quarantine queue size 8\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: globals (start-address=0xe7ee68e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: constants (start-address=0xe7ebe8e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: heap (start-address=0xe6ebe8e00000 size=1024 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: stack (start-address=0xe6cbe8e00000 size=128 GiB)\r\n\r\nKLEE: done: total instructions = 10\r\nKLEE: done: completed paths = 1\r\nKLEE: done: partially completed paths = 1\r\nKLEE: done: generated tests = 2\r\nRC=0\r\nassembly.ll\r\ninfo\r\nmessages.txt\r\nrun.istats\r\nrun.stats\r\ntest000001.assert.err\r\ntest000001.kquery\r\ntest000001.ktest\r\ntest000002.ktest\r\nwarnings.txt\r\nKLEE: Using STP solver backend\r\nKLEE: SAT solver: MiniSat\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: Using quarantine queue size 8\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: globals (start-address=0xe91368e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: constants (start-address=0xe910e8e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: heap (start-address=0xe810e8e00000 size=1024 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: stack (start-address=0xe7f0e8e00000 size=128 GiB)\r\nKLEE: ERROR: /tmp/test_klee.c:7: ASSERTION FAIL: 0\r\nKLEE: NOTE: now ignoring this error at this location\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: Using quarantine queue size 8\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: globals (start-address=0xe7ee68e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: constants (start-address=0xe7ebe8e00000 size=10 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: heap (start-address=0xe6ebe8e00000 size=1024 GiB)\r\nKLEE: Deterministic allocator: stack (start-address=0xe6cbe8e00000 size=128 GiB)\r\n\r\n"]
