[176.70779, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m18\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[176.708349, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe solver and header paths are correct, and KLEE successfully used STP/MiniSat. I'll now prepend a robust environment block to `~/.bashrc` so `PATH`, `CPATH`, \r\nand the runtime library path are configured even for non-interactive shell sourcing.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -eux; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\np = Path.home() / \".bashrc\"\r\ntext = p.read_text()\r\nmarker = \"# KLEE installation environment\"\r\nif marker not in text:\r\n    block = '''# KLEE installation environment\r\n# Make KLEE binaries and headers available to all shells.\r\nexport PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:${PATH}\"\r\nexport CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:${CPATH}}\"\r\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}\"\r\nexport KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=\"/usr/local/include\"\r\n\r\n'''\r\n    # Must be before Ubuntu's non-interactive-shell early return.\r\n    p.write_text(block + text)\r\nPY\r\nnl -ba ~/.bashrc | sed -n '1,20p'; echo '--- fresh noninteractive source'; bash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; echo PATH=\"$PATH\"; echo CPATH=\"$CPATH\"; echo \r\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"; echo KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=\"$KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR\"; command -v klee; command -v stp; klee --version'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[176.709957, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[176.744622, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[176.746017, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n+ python3 -\r\n+ nl -ba /root/.bashrc\r\n+ sed -n 1,20p\r\n     1  # KLEE installation environment\r\n     2  # Make KLEE binaries and headers available to all shells.\r\n     3  export PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:${PATH}\"\r\n     4  export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:${CPATH}}\"\r\n     5  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}\"\r\n     6  export KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=\"/usr/local/include\"\r\n     7  \r\n     8  # ~/.bashrc: executed by bash(1) for non-login shells.\r\n     9  # see /usr/share/doc/bash/examples/startup-files (in the package bash-doc)\r\n    10  # for examples\r\n    11  \r\n    12  # If not running interactively, don't do anything\r\n    13  [ -z \"$PS1\" ] && return\r\n    14  \r\n    15  # don't put duplicate lines in the history. See bash(1) for more options\r\n"]
[176.746092, "o", "    16  # ... or force ignoredups and ignorespace\r\n    17  HISTCONTROL=ignoredups:ignorespace\r\n    18  \r\n    19  # append to the history file, don't overwrite it\r\n    20  shopt -s histappend\r\n+ echo --- fresh noninteractive source\r\n--- fresh noninteractive source\r\n+ bash -c source ~/.bashrc; echo PATH=\"$PATH\"; echo CPATH=\"$CPATH\"; echo LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"; echo KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=\"$KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR\"; command \r\n-v klee; command -v stp; klee --version\r\nPATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\r\nCPATH=/usr/local/include\r\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib\r\nKLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=/usr/local/include\r\n/usr/local/bin/klee\r\n/usr/local/bin/stp\r\n"]
[176.746109, "o", "KLEE 3.3 (https://klee-se.org/)\r\n  Build mode: Release (Asserts: OFF)\r\n  Build revision: 74f49f1d243f0e1692a00ac688a7b805b37c5646\r\n\r\nUbuntu LLVM version 16.0.6\r\n  Optimized build.\r\n\r\n"]
