[199.130381, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m20\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2KThe end-to-end run works with both the default and explicit STP/MiniSat settings. To be maximally robust for header discovery, I'll add both \r\n`/usr/local/include` (for `<klee/klee.h>`) and `/usr/local/include/klee` (for `<klee.h>`) to `CPATH`, then re-verify environment loading.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -eux; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\np = Path.home() / \".bashrc\"\r\ntext = p.read_text()\r\nold = 'export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:${CPATH}}\"\\n'\r\nnew = 'export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee${CPATH:+:${CPATH}}\"\\n'\r\nif old not in text:\r\n    raise SystemExit(\"expected CPATH line not found\")\r\np.write_text(text.replace(old, new, 1))\r\nPY\r\ngrep -n 'export PATH\\|export CPATH\\|export LD_LIBRARY_PATH\\|KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR' ~/.bashrc | head -10\r\nbash -c 'source ~/.bashrc; echo \"PATH=$PATH\"; echo \"CPATH=$CPATH\"; command -v klee; printf \"#include <klee/klee.h>\\n#include <klee.h>\\nint main(void){return \r\n0;}\\n\" >/tmp/header_test.c; clang-16 -fsyntax-only /tmp/header_test.c; echo HEADER_TEST_OK'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[199.130901, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[199.237069, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[199.237661, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n+ python3 -\r\n+ grep -n export PATH\\|export CPATH\\|export LD_LIBRARY_PATH\\|KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR /root/.bashrc\r\n+ head -10\r\n3:export PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:${PATH}\"\r\n4:export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee${CPATH:+:${CPATH}}\"\r\n5:export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}\"\r\n6:export KLEE_INCLUDE_DIR=\"/usr/local/include\"\r\n+ bash -c source ~/.bashrc; echo \"PATH=$PATH\"; echo \"CPATH=$CPATH\"; command -v klee; printf \"#include <klee/klee.h>\\n#include <klee.h>\\nint main(void){return \r\n0;}\\n\" >/tmp/header_test.c; clang-16 -fsyntax-only /tmp/header_test.c; echo HEADER_TEST_OK\r\nPATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\r\nCPATH=/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee\r\n/usr/local/bin/klee\r\nHEADER_TEST_OK\r\n\r\n"]
[199.241718, "o", "\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
